{"content_hash": "e9c03ba8e1e076d1", "version_id": 564, "article_id": 57, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Russia hits Zaporizhzhia with glide bombs, killing 20", "title_zh": "俄罗斯用滑翔炸弹袭击扎波罗热，至少20人死亡", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwvgdpv642g5o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1765180520768-aa3ef0ea7b37?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8M3x8cnVzc2lhbiUyMGdsaWRlJTIwYm9tYnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNjc4MzEwfDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Alex Ko on Unsplash", "author": "Alex Ko", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@alexko?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/aeroflot-airplane-on-the-tarmac-at-an-airport-MPK9BSV2mok?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(169, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(207, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "ac39eda995dc"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-10", "word_count": 232, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "Russia attacked the Ukrainian city of Zaporizhzhia with five glide bombs, killing at least 20 people, including four children. The attack came after the US eased sanctions on Russian diesel.", "lead_zh": "俄罗斯用五枚滑翔炸弹袭击了乌克兰城市扎波罗热，造成至少20人死亡，其中包括四名儿童。此次袭击发生在美国放松对俄罗斯柴油制裁之后。", "preview": "On Saturday morning, Russian glide bombs hit residential buildings in Zaporizhzhia, a southern city with over 700,000 residents. Local offic", "preview_zh": "周六上午，俄罗斯滑翔炸弹击中了扎波罗热南部的居民楼。当地官员称，至少20人死亡，其中包括四名儿童，另有32人受伤。还有更多人失踪，据信被困在废墟下。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 550, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/57/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 89.987, "size_bytes": 543600, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 257, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/564.json", "paragraphs": ["On Saturday morning, Russian glide bombs hit residential buildings in Zaporizhzhia, a southern city with over 700,000 residents. Local officials said at least 20 people were killed, including four children, and 32 others were injured. More people are still missing and believed to be trapped under the rubble.", "Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said the attack showed Russia's \"thanks\" for a deal announced by US President Donald Trump last night, which eased sanctions on Moscow to import Russian diesel. He added that 13 other regions were attacked overnight, proving Russia takes any easing of pressure as a sign it can keep fighting.", "Acting Mayor Regina Harchenko told Ukrainian television from the scene that the ground floor was hit and the floors above collapsed. More than 80 workers are involved in search and rescue operations, which are expected to continue all day. Rescuers regularly stop to listen for noises from survivors under the rubble.", "Zaporizhzhia is less than 10 miles from the front line and is frequently attacked by Russian drones and missiles. Both Russia and Ukraine have stepped up attacks on infrastructure in recent months. On Thursday, at least 33 people were killed in a glide bomb attack on two buses in Kramatorsk, and on Wednesday, 22 people died in a missile strike in Pryluky. The UN says civilian casualties in Ukraine jumped by 55% in the first eight months of this year."], "paragraphs_zh": ["周六上午，俄罗斯滑翔炸弹击中了扎波罗热南部的居民楼。当地官员称，至少20人死亡，其中包括四名儿童，另有32人受伤。还有更多人失踪，据信被困在废墟下。", "乌克兰总统泽连斯基表示，这次袭击表明俄罗斯对美国总统特朗普昨晚宣布的协议表示“感谢”，该协议放松了对莫斯科进口俄罗斯柴油的制裁。他还说，另有13个地区在夜间遭到袭击，证明俄罗斯把任何压力放松都视为可以继续战斗的信号。", "代理市长哈尔琴科在乌克兰电视台上从现场表示，一楼被击中，上面的楼层坍塌了。超过80名工作人员参与搜救行动，预计将持续一整天。救援人员经常停下来倾听废墟下幸存者发出的声音。", "扎波罗热距离前线不到10英里，经常遭到俄罗斯无人机和导弹袭击。近几个月来，俄罗斯和乌克兰都加大了对基础设施的袭击。周四，克拉马托尔斯克的两辆巴士遭滑翔炸弹袭击，至少33人死亡；周三，普里卢基遭导弹袭击，22人死亡。联合国称，今年前八个月乌克兰平民伤亡人数增加了55%。"], "body": "On Saturday morning, Russian glide bombs hit residential buildings in Zaporizhzhia, a southern city with over 700,000 residents. Local officials said at least 20 people were killed, including four children, and 32 others were injured. More people are still missing and believed to be trapped under the rubble.\n\nUkrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said the attack showed Russia's \"thanks\" for a deal announced by US President Donald Trump last night, which eased sanctions on Moscow to import Russian diesel. He added that 13 other regions were attacked overnight, proving Russia takes any easing of pressure as a sign it can keep fighting.\n\nActing Mayor Regina Harchenko told Ukrainian television from the scene that the ground floor was hit and the floors above collapsed. More than 80 workers are involved in search and rescue operations, which are expected to continue all day. Rescuers regularly stop to listen for noises from survivors under the rubble.\n\nZaporizhzhia is less than 10 miles from the front line and is frequently attacked by Russian drones and missiles. Both Russia and Ukraine have stepped up attacks on infrastructure in recent months. On Thursday, at least 33 people were killed in a glide bomb attack on two buses in Kramatorsk, and on Wednesday, 22 people died in a missile strike in Pryluky. The UN says civilian casualties in Ukraine jumped by 55% in the first eight months of this year.", "body_zh": "周六上午，俄罗斯滑翔炸弹击中了扎波罗热南部的居民楼。当地官员称，至少20人死亡，其中包括四名儿童，另有32人受伤。还有更多人失踪，据信被困在废墟下。\n\n乌克兰总统泽连斯基表示，这次袭击表明俄罗斯对美国总统特朗普昨晚宣布的协议表示“感谢”，该协议放松了对莫斯科进口俄罗斯柴油的制裁。他还说，另有13个地区在夜间遭到袭击，证明俄罗斯把任何压力放松都视为可以继续战斗的信号。\n\n代理市长哈尔琴科在乌克兰电视台上从现场表示，一楼被击中，上面的楼层坍塌了。超过80名工作人员参与搜救行动，预计将持续一整天。救援人员经常停下来倾听废墟下幸存者发出的声音。\n\n扎波罗热距离前线不到10英里，经常遭到俄罗斯无人机和导弹袭击。近几个月来，俄罗斯和乌克兰都加大了对基础设施的袭击。周四，克拉马托尔斯克的两辆巴士遭滑翔炸弹袭击，至少33人死亡；周三，普里卢基遭导弹袭击，22人死亡。联合国称，今年前八个月乌克兰平民伤亡人数增加了55%。", "text": "On Saturday morning, Russian glide bombs hit residential buildings in Zaporizhzhia, a southern city with over 700,000 residents. Local officials said at least 20 people were killed, including four children, and 32 others were injured. More people are still missing and believed to be trapped under the rubble. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said the attack showed Russia's \"thanks\" for a deal announced by US President Donald Trump last night, which eased sanctions on Moscow to import Russian diesel. He added that 13 other regions were attacked overnight, proving Russia takes any easing of pressure as a sign it can keep fighting. Acting Mayor Regina Harchenko told Ukrainian television from the scene that the ground floor was hit and the floors above collapsed. More than 80 workers are involved in search and rescue operations, which are expected to continue all day. Rescuers regularly stop to listen for noises from survivors under the rubble. Zaporizhzhia is less than 10 miles from the front line and is frequently attacked by Russian drones and missiles. Both Russia and Ukraine have stepped up attacks on infrastructure in recent months. On Thursday, at least 33 people were killed in a glide bomb attack on two buses in Kramatorsk, and on Wednesday, 22 people died in a missile strike in Pryluky. The UN says civilian casualties in Ukraine jumped by 55% in the first eight months of this year.", "vocab": [{"word": "glide bomb", "pos": "noun", "zh": "滑翔炸弹", "note": "一种带翼的炸弹，能滑翔较长距离", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "residential", "pos": "adj", "zh": "住宅的", "note": "常用来描述建筑或区域", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rubble", "pos": "noun", "zh": "瓦砾，废墟", "note": "建筑物倒塌后的碎片", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "ease", "pos": "verb", "zh": "放松，减轻", "note": "此处指放松制裁", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "sanction", "pos": "noun", "zh": "制裁", "note": "常以复数形式出现", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "overnight", "pos": "adv", "zh": "一夜之间", "note": "表示在夜间发生", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "acting mayor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "代理市长", "note": "临时担任市长职务的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "collapse", "pos": "verb", "zh": "倒塌", "note": "建筑物等坍塌", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "survivor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "幸存者", "note": "从灾难中活下来的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "front line", "pos": "noun", "zh": "前线", "note": "战争中最接近敌人的地带", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "casualty", "pos": "noun", "zh": "伤亡人员", "note": "常指死伤者", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "jump", "pos": "verb", "zh": "猛增", "note": "表示数量突然增加", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Russian glide bomb attack on Zaporizhzhia kills at least 20 people", "summary_original": "Volodymyr Zelensky says the attack, which left children dead, was Russia expressing its \"thanks\" for a US diesel deal.", "body_original": "Russian glide bomb attack on Zaporizhzhia kills at least 20 people\nBy\nVitaly Shevchenko\nand\nTom McArthur\nPublished\n10 October 2026\nRussia has attacked the Ukrainian city of Zaporizhzhia with five glide bombs, killing at least 20 people including four children, local officials said.\nThe glide bombs hit residential buildings in the southern city on Saturday morning. At least\n32 others were injured in the attack, with more still missing and believed to be under the rubble.\nUkrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said the attacks on Zaporizhzhia were Russia expressing \"its thanks\" for a deal announced by US President Donald Trump last night easing sanctions on Moscow to import Russian diesel.\nHe added that 13 other regions had come under attack overnight, arguing this demonstrated Russia took \"any easing of pressure to mean they can keep fighting\".\nPhotos and videos from the site of one of the strikes in Zaporizhzhia show an apartment block mostly destroyed.\n\"The ground floor was hit, and the floors above just collapsed,\" acting Mayor Regina Harchenko told Ukrainian television from the scene.\nShe said more than 80 workers were involved in ongoing search and rescue operations which are expected to continue throughout the day.\nThe rescuers regularly stop to listen for any noises made by survivors who could be under the rubble.\nHarchenko said Russia had struck at \"our very heart\" and \"our littlest ones\" were among those killed, adding that their deaths were \"awful grief for their families. For the city.\"\nZaporizhzhia is a major regional centre with more than 700,000 residents. It is located less than 10 miles (16km) from the front line\nand is frequently attacked by Russian drones and missiles\n.\nTrump announces deal for Russian diesel as Zelensky calls it a gift to Putin\nPublished\n9 hours ago\nAnalysis: Trump's shock Russia deal highlights mounting pressure to curb fuel prices\nPublished\n1 day ago\nZelensky was quick to criticise Trump's diesel deal with Russia, calling it\na gift to Russian President Vladimir Putin\n. Analysts view the deal as an attempt by the US president to allay domestic concerns about high fuel prices ahead of the upcoming midterm elections.\nZelensky wrote on social media on Saturday that Russian attacks on energy facilities in the capital, Kyiv, demonstrated Russia's \"true intentions\".\n\"Russia's choice is war. And they will be ready to end it only when they feel that their ability to drag the war out is diminishing.\n\"Unfortunately, the signals Russia received yesterday were entirely different – signals suggesting that it could simply keep attacking. And this needs to be corrected.\"\nBoth Russia and Ukraine have stepped up attacks on infrastructure in recent months, as Moscow's full-scale invasion, launched in 2022, drags on.\nOn Thursday, at least 33 people were killed in another Russian glide bomb attack on two civilian buses in Kramatorsk, in the eastern Donetsk region.\nThe day before,\n22 people including five children\ndied as a Russian missile hit an apartment block in the town of Pryluky, east of Kyiv.\nThe number of civilian casualties in Ukraine\njumped by 55%\n,\nexternal\nin the first eight months of this year, according to the UN.\nRussia has\nalso stepped up its attacks on Ukrainian energy infrastructure\nas winter approaches, a strategy it has undertaken in previous years. Kyiv has repeatedly accused it of targeting Ukraine's civilian population, which Moscow denies.\nFor its part, Ukraine has increasingly adopted a policy of striking infrastructure often deep inside Russia that is crucial to its economy, including several oil refineries and terminals.\nSeveral\nstrikes on data centres owned by Yandex\nhave left the tech giant struggling to maintain services.\nKyiv says its strikes are aimed at curtailing revenue streams for Russia's war machine.\nRelated topics\nWar in Ukraine\nUkraine\nMore on this story\nWatch: Fleeing Kyiv for the countryside ahead of winter\nPublished\n1 day ago\nFear and disruption for Ukraine's rail passengers as Russia escalates drone attacks\nPublished\n4 days ago\nRussia targeting 'ordinary life' with attacks on Ukraine's data centres, Zelensky says\nPublished\n25 September", "fetched_at": "2026-10-11T00:25:09.061571", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "On", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.338, "sm": 100, "em": 337, "cs": 0, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Saturday", "s": 0.35, "e": 0.812, "sm": 350, "em": 812, "cs": 3, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "morning", "s": 0.825, "e": 1.237, "sm": 825, "em": 1237, "cs": 12, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": ",", "s": 1.237, "e": 1.512, "sm": 1237, "em": 1512, "cs": 19, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "Russian", "s": 1.512, "e": 1.837, "sm": 1512, "em": 1837, "cs": 21, "ce": 28, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "glide", "s": 1.85, "e": 2.2, "sm": 1850, "em": 2200, "cs": 29, "ce": 34, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "bombs", "s": 2.212, "e": 2.6, "sm": 2212, "em": 2600, "cs": 35, "ce": 40, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "hit", "s": 2.612, "e": 2.85, "sm": 2612, "em": 2849, "cs": 41, "ce": 44, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "residential", "s": 2.862, "e": 3.45, "sm": 2862, "em": 3449, "cs": 45, "ce": 56, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "buildings", "s": 3.462, "e": 3.887, "sm": 3462, "em": 3887, "cs": 57,